fetch by fingerprint, not by email.

================================================================
attribution policy
================================================================

Every artifact in this repository, code, comments, commit messages,
documentation, error strings, configuration files, is authored by the
maintainer.  No file references generative tooling, vendor names
behind such tooling, or any "generated", "co-authored", or "with help
from" attribution phrasing.  The forbidden-token list is enforced by
the repository's pre-commit attribution scan.

If you contribute a patch, sign your work under the
Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO) by adding a Signed-off-by line
to your commit.  See docs/CONTRIBUTING.md for the full process.

================================================================
license, per file category
================================================================

Every file in this tarball is authored by the maintainer and falls
into one of the categories below.  Each category has a single,
explicit license; that license applies to every file in the category.

  (1) Source code: .el, .c, .h, .scm, .sh, .yml, .py, .conf, .mk, and
      every file named "Makefile".  Licensed under the GNU General
      Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).  Each
      such file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header AND the
      complete GPL notice paragraph in the file's own comment style.
      Canonical license text in COPYING at the repository root.

  (2) Documentation: every .md file in the tree (README, CHANGELOG,
      docs/*.md, docs/runlogs/*.md, docs/upstream/*.md,
      docs/savannah/*.md).  Licensed under the GNU Free Documentation
      License, version 1.3 or later (GFDL-1.3-or-later), with no
      Invariant Sections, no Front-Cover Texts, and no Back-Cover
      Texts.  Each .md file carries a visible "## license" section at
      the end with the canonical GFDL notice paragraph, and a
      machine-readable SPDX comment at the top.  Canonical license
      text in COPYING.DOC at the repository root.

  (3) Upstream patches: docs/upstream/patches/*.patch.  These are
      patches authored by the maintainer against upstream projects
      (currently a single patch against GNU Emacs).  Each patch
      inherits the license of the project it modifies; the Emacs
      patch is therefore GPL-3.0-or-later.  The patch metadata
      (From/Date/Subject headers) is part of the standard
      git-format-patch envelope and is not separately licensed.

  (4) Upstream-correspondence drafts: docs/upstream/emails/*.txt.
      These are drafts of messages the maintainer wrote and sent to
      upstream mailing lists (bug-hurd, debian-hurd, bug-gnu-emacs).
      Licensed under the GNU Free Documentation License, version 1.3
      or later (GFDL-1.3-or-later), with no Invariant Sections, no
      Front-Cover Texts, and no Back-Cover Texts.  The license is
      documented for the whole subdirectory in
      docs/upstream/STATUS.md rather than per-file, because adding a
      notice header inside an .eml-style file would break its email
      format if the file is later re-fed into a mail client.

  (5) Binary media: docs/img/*.png and docs/runlogs/*.png.
      Inventoried per-file in docs/MEDIA.md with origin and license.
      Maintainer-authored logos and serial-console screenshots are
      licensed under GFDL-1.3-or-later, matching the documentation
      license.

  (6) License texts: COPYING (GPL 3.0 verbatim) and COPYING.DOC
      (GFDL 1.3 verbatim).  These are the published license texts
      from the Free Software Foundation; they are not separately
      licensed.

  (7) Project metadata: AUTHORS (this file).  Licensed under
      GFDL-1.3-or-later, matching the documentation license.

For the complete file-by-file inventory of categories (1) through
(5), see "git ls-files" combined with docs/MEDIA.md (category 5) and
docs/upstream/STATUS.md (categories 3 and 4).

================================================================
license, for redistributors
================================================================

A distributor wishing to repackage GEOS should:

  - keep COPYING and COPYING.DOC at the root of the redistribution
    (they are the license texts the per-file notices refer to);
  - preserve the SPDX headers, full notice paragraphs, and
    "## license" footers on the files that already carry them;
  - preserve docs/MEDIA.md and docs/upstream/STATUS.md, which
    document the legal status of files where a per-file notice would
    be technically inappropriate (binary assets, email archives).

The contribution policy in CONTRIBUTING.md requires an FSF copyright
assignment for every contributor; until that paperwork is on file for
a given contributor, their patches will not be merged.  The maintainer
is the sole copyright holder of every commit in the repository to
date.
